"Counted with the original on-effort group" is also a statement about
distance. \code{distance = "with_group"} (the default) reads it literally: the
animals \emph{are} that group, and a group has one distance, one detection
probability and one row. The animals are added to its \code{NUMBER} and no
second observation is made. This is right only where the animals really are
that group or associated with it, which is what \code{mode = "same_species"}
tests.

\code{distance = "break_off"} reads the sighting as its own, with a distance
from the census line at the break-off:
\itemize{
\item Where the record carries an exact position (\code{S_LAT}/\code{S_LONG}), that
